These are implementation evidence because MediaWiki returned the memberships and they are preserved in <code>archive-v1/index.json</code>.

Source recovery is much richer. Common <code>Has entity type</code> source values include Idea, Project, Implementation, Concept, Event, Person, Topic, Organization, Publication, Protocol, Dataset, Location, and Technology, but also page/system-role terms such as Index, Ontology, Governance, Documentation, Schema-Matter, Front-Matter, Research, and Validation.

That mixture is a direct warning against copying V1 source values into one V2 entity vocabulary.

Source annotations may also appear inside examples/specifications. They are source-syntax evidence, not a complete exported SMW semantic-store snapshot.

== Topic decomposition test ==

Topic-associated source syntax appears in several functions:

* domain / field signal — 43 occurrences;
* hierarchy or Topic-relation signal — 22 occurrences;
* entity/page-type use of <code>Topic</code> — 9 occurrences.

The exact counts include documentation/specification syntax; their architectural value is qualitative: '''Topic was visibly doing several different jobs.'''

Current V2 separates those jobs into:

* [[Property:Domain|Domain]] — subject/field membership;
* Entity type — primary modeled identity;
* Category / Portal / index / outline — human navigation;
* explicit Relationships — graph semantics;
* Book Matter — reusable content anatomy.

The corpus therefore supports the decomposition recorded in [[BITwiki:V1 ontology maturation]] rather than restoration of one overloaded Topic primitive.

