This is the strongest corpus result so far.

'''V1 Main was primarily a laboratory for BITwiki itself: architecture, epistemics, schema, composition, navigation, validation, and governance. It was not a 162-article encyclopedia awaiting reclassification.'''

== First-class subject evidence ==

Only two historical pages currently qualify as coherent first-class subject/project candidates:

* <code>Bioluminescent Organisms</code>;
* <code>Fluorescent Coral Reefs</code>.

Both are composed parent pages with transcluded subpages, providing direct implementation evidence for the V1 composability/Book Matter idea.

The role audit deliberately does not finalize their V2 entity types. Bioluminescent Organisms carries an old <code>Ideas</code> signal, while Fluorescent Coral Reefs mixes implementation/project language. Those are questions for canonicalization, not mechanical migration.

== Reusable subject signal ==

The 52 composition artifacts contain real subject/method/protocol/evidence signal even though the historical artifacts themselves are Book Matter.

Notable examples:

* Emergence — concept definition fragment;
* Feedback-loop — concept definition fragment;
* Homeostasis — concept definition fragment;
* Systems-analysis — method fragment;
* Peer-review-protocol — protocol fragment;
* Validation-procedure — protocol fragment;
* Empirical-validation — evidence-summary fragment;
* Peer-review-summary — evidence-summary fragment.

This supports current broad V2 patterns such as Concept, Method, Protocol, and explicit evidence/epistemic structures without requiring the fragments themselves to become top-level ontology objects.

== What the evidence authorizes ==

The current corpus evidence is strong enough to retain the following architectural conclusions:

# Entity type, Domain, navigation, Book Matter, epistemics/lifecycle, and Relationships must remain independent dimensions.
# V1 Topic should not be restored as one universal primitive.
# Page role must be separated from subject ontology.
# V1 categories cannot be migrated mechanically into V2 semantic identity.
# V1 source-level type values mix ontology, page role, system role, and documentation role and require contextual disposition.
# Book Matter/transclusion have direct implementation evidence, not merely design intent.
# The current V2 exemplars plus the two V1 first-class subject pages are still insufficient to freeze the final Entity type or Domain vocabularies.
# Architecture sources and historical branches are valuable lineage, not disposable meta-content.

== Next empirical work ==

The evidence now splits the migration into two clean streams.

=== Subject canonicalization ===

Review the two first-class subject pages and reusable subject fragments against their full revision/source lineage. Determine:

* canonical object boundaries;
* mature Entity type and Domain values;
* which secondary roles belong in relationships rather than multiple types;
* what Book Matter should remain independently reusable;
* what citations, uncertainty, and provenance must survive;
* whether repeated unresolved patterns justify new ontology terms.

=== Architecture maturation ===

Group the 83 architecture/system sources by design family—ontology, epistemics, confidence, templates, schema, governance, constitutional writing, navigation, research systems, etc.—and mature each through the [[BITwiki:V1 maturation register]].

The subject corpus should test the architecture; the architecture corpus should not impersonate subject ontology.

== Reproducibility ==

Run:

<pre>
python scripts/validate_v2.py
python scripts/inventory_corpus.py
python scripts/classify_v1_page_roles.py
</pre>

Pull-request validation runs all three and uploads the generated evidence files as a workflow artifact.

